# Contributing to {{REPO_NAME}}

Read first: `../{{DOCS_REPO}}/docs/onboarding.md`, then `AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, `docs/rules/`.

## Workflow
- Pick an issue labelled `ready-for-agent` or `ready-for-human`; branch from `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}`; PR with `Closes #n`. Never push to `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}`.
- No secrets, `.env` files or personal data in commits, issues, PRs or AI chats.

## Commands
| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `{{BUILD_CMD}}` | Build every function (arm64) |
| `{{TEST_CMD}}` | Unit tests |
| `{{LINT_CMD}}` | Lint |
| `{{SECURITY_CMD}}` | Security scan |
| `{{INTEGRATION_CMD}}` | Template validation |

Do not deploy from your machine. Staging deploys from CI; production only through the release workflow.

## Adding a function
Skills `add-lambda`, `add-schedule`, `s3-storage`.

## Required checks
`lint`, `test`, `validate`, `security`; deploy jobs depend on them in the same run.

## Editing agents
Edit only `agents/<name>.md`, run `python3 scripts/sync-agents.py`, commit generated files.
